## 6. Build & Deploy

1. `mvn clean package`
2. Copy the shaded JAR to your Connect worker `plugin.path`
3. Restart Connect
4. POST connector config via REST:

```json
{
  "name": "cassandra-commitlog-src",
  "config": {
    "connector.class": "com.example.cdc.CassandraCommitLogConnector",
    "tasks.max": "1",
    "cassandra.contact.points": "127.0.0.1",
    "cassandra.port": "9042",
    "cassandra.keyspace.whitelist": "sales",
    "tables.whitelist": "company",
    "cdc.dir": "/var/lib/cassandra/data/cdc_raw"
  }
}
```

This setup will tail each new `.cdc` file in the `cdc_raw_directory`, parse mutations, and emit `SourceRecord`s to Kafka topics `cdc_sales.company` in near real time.  You can extend serialization, error handling, and parallelism by splitting token-ranges across tasks.  Enjoy your custom, production-grade connector!
